+## 119. Interface invariants of rhombohedral graphene under layer potentials and couplings
+
+**Source:** Yuelong Li, “Interface invariants of rhombohedral graphene with layer-dependent potentials and couplings.” arXiv:2611.29093, 21 November 2026 (cond-mat.mes-hall). Domain walls in the perpendicular bias of ABC-stacked graphene bind valley-resolved chiral modes whose signed number is fixed by a bulk-difference invariant. The invariant equals the difference of occupied angular weights of the zero-momentum levels. At equal coupling, nonlinear monotone potentials reproduce the same invariant set as linear potentials; bond-dependent coupling fills gaps inside that set beginning at five layers without enlarging the range. Exact transfer-matrix calculations reproduce every predicted signed crossing count. Code: https://github.com/YuelongLi/RHG_Spectral_Indices
+
+**Loop:** Layer-potential and coupling residual → cut by zero-momentum angular-weight occupation → residual: bulk-difference invariant of interface modes → closed by combinatorial characterization of admissible configurations and exact spectral matching.
